A table dropped on purpose that others still refer to: every step runs,
then the foreign key check before the commit finds the rows pointing
nowhere, and it all rolls back.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE course (dish_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES dish (id), menu_id INTEGER REFERENCES menu (id)) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1);
INSERT INTO course VALUES (1, 1);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE course (dish_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES dish (id), menu_id INTEGER REFERENCES menu (id)) STRICT;
-- @drop table menu

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 1 step
  table `menu`: dropped on purpose
    DROP TABLE "menu"

== error
migrating test.db: rows that would break a foreign key: 1 (PRAGMA foreign_key_check names them)
